      "writtenOn": "2025-10-07T12:24:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nice use of ** for the side note ^^\n\nThe intention is that `webgpu.h` is ABI compatible and like you said, it cannot contain std::function etc. The backdoor headers `DawnNative.h` and `*Backend.h` don\u0027t have this constraint though and can be used to define some of the extension structs (like [this one](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/include/dawn/native/D3D12Backend.h;drc\u003da50d9ba592fb030943387f315b74ed6250be9835;l\u003d56)).\n\nYour idea of returning a `wgpu::Future` is pretty great IMHO and since it can be waited on and queried with `WaitAny` it seems that it could work well for Chromium\u0027s usecase! +CC Loko to see if he\u0027s got any concerns adding a future for \"WaitUntilScheduled\".",
